{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothNormalisation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RothNormalisation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothContradiction"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.hfin_of_large","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.hfin_of_large","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothNormalisation.lean#L272-L278","doc":"**The last inequality, discharged.**  `(1+θ)·m·L' < K(μ−ν)` under the standard relations\n`K = (2+δ)L`, `L' = (1+η)L`, `μ = m(½−ε)`, given the `m` that `exists_m_of_slack` produces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_m_of_slack","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_m_of_slack","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothNormalisation.lean#L258-L270","doc":"**Take `m` large.**  Once the slack budget balances, an `m` making the inequality strict\nexists — and this is the only place in Roth's theorem where \"sufficiently large\" is used for its\nArchimedean content rather than as shorthand for a counting bound.\n\nNo sign condition on `ν` is needed; I wrote one and the linter reported it unused, which is right —\n`exists_nat_gt` does not care.  The stronger statement is kept. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.slack_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.slack_pos","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothNormalisation.lean#L251-L256","doc":"**When the slack budget balances.**  The bracket that has to be positive before enlarging `m`\nhelps at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.roth_contradiction_of_normalisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.roth_contradiction_of_normalisation","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothNormalisation.lean#L187-L223","doc":"**Step 4 from the normalisation.**  `roth_contradiction` with its additive hypothesis replaced\nby data a parameter choice can actually be checked against: an upper normalisation `r_h·log q_h ≤\nL'`, a per-coordinate size condition, and one comparison of constants.\n\nThe remaining `hfin` is Roth's inequality with everything named: `(1+θ)·m·L'` on the left — the\ndenominators' total size inflated by the polynomial's `θ`-share — against `K·(μ−ν)` on the right,\nthe approximation exponent times the index gap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.height_le_den","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.height_le_den","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothNormalisation.lean#L157-L179","doc":"**What recovers the lower half.**  If the numerator does not exceed the denominator then the\nheight of the reduced fraction is at most `q`, so `log H_h ≤ log q_h` and the normalisation's\nlower bound transfers from heights to denominators.\n\nNote it is the *reduced* fraction's height: `2/4` has height `2`, not `4`, which is why this is an\ninequality rather than the equality `H_h = q_h` one might expect. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.rothDegrees_log_bounds_den","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.rothDegrees_log_bounds_den","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothNormalisation.lean#L138-L155","doc":"**The normalisation in the denominators' currency, and what does not transfer.**  Step 4 wants\nbounds on `r_h·log q_h`, but `rothDegrees` is built from the *heights* `H_h = max(|p_h|, q_h)`.\nThe **upper** half transfers for free, because `q_h ≤ H_h`.\n\nThe **lower** half does not, and the asymmetry is real rather than an artefact: `H_h ≤ q_h` fails\nwhenever the numerator dominates, and then `r_h·log q_h` sits arbitrarily far below `r_h·log H_h`.\n`height_le_den` below identifies exactly what recovers it — `|p_h| ≤ q_h`, which in Roth's setting\nis the harmless consequence of approximating a number of absolute value at most `1`.  It is a\nhypothesis on the approximations, not a consequence of the degree choice, and stating which one\nis the point of separating these two lemmas. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.rothDegrees_log_bounds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.rothDegrees_log_bounds","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothNormalisation.lean#L106-L136","doc":"**`rothDegrees` is two-sided.**  `r_h = log_{H_h} N` (plus one off the first coordinate) puts\n`r_h·log H_h` within `log H_h` of `log N` on both sides — so the degrees `Γ_m`'s growth clause is\nbuilt from already satisfy the normalisation step 4's inequality needs.  The two halves of the\nargument were never using different normalisations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.log_taylorConst_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.log_taylorConst_le","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothNormalisation.lean#L71-L100","doc":"**The polynomial's size, bounded per coordinate.**  `2 + c_H + log(4B) ≤ θ·log q_h` — each\ndenominator large compared with the per-degree cost — gives\n`log(taylorConst) ≤ θ·∑_h r_h·log q_h`.\n\n`c_H` is the rate at which step 1's height bound grows with `∑_h r_h`; taking it as a hypothesis\nrather than deriving it keeps this file independent of which Siegel lemma produced the\npolynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.log_condition_of_cost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.log_condition_of_cost","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothNormalisation.lean#L53-L69","doc":"**The upper half of the normalisation does the work.**  With `∑_h r_h·log q_h ≤ m·L'` and the\npolynomial's size a `θ`-fraction of it, the additive form of Roth's inequality reduces to a\ncomparison of constants. ","signatureChunk":0}]}